@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/cka-theme.puml
title A selector is a filter: the ReplicaSet counts only the Pods that match

rectangle "ReplicaSet\n<size:11>replicas: 3</size>\n<size:11>selector: tier=front-end</size>" <<accent>> as rs

rectangle "Pods in the same namespace" <<group>> as pods {
  rectangle "web-a\n<size:11>tier=front-end</size>" <<good>> as a
  rectangle "web-b\n<size:11>tier=front-end</size>" <<good>> as b
  rectangle "bare-pod\n<size:11>tier=front-end</size>\n<size:11>created by hand earlier</size>" <<good>> as c
  rectangle "db\n<size:11>tier=back-end</size>" <<muted>> as d
  rectangle "cache\n<size:11>no tier label</size>" <<muted>> as e
  a -[hidden]right-> b
  b -[hidden]right-> c
  c -[hidden]right-> d
  d -[hidden]right-> e
}

rs -down-> a
rs -down-> b
rs -down-> c

caption <i>3 matching Pods = desired state, so nothing is created. The hand-made Pod is acquired, and the template is used only when a replacement is needed.</i>\n<i>Add a fourth matching Pod and the ReplicaSet deletes one. Change a Pod's label and it stops counting, so a new Pod is created.</i>
@enduml
